cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the KPM-1 election projections in your research, please cite
  the underlying DYNAMICS-8 persona framework AND the more recent KPM v17.10
  methodology paper. KPM-1 is preserved here as the first-generation
  pre-registered baseline; KPM v17.10 is the current production methodology.
type: dataset
title: "KPM-1 — Pre-Registered Synthetic-Panel UK Council Election Projections (May 2026)"
abstract: >-
  KPM-1: the first-generation Kronaxis Polling Method. Pre-registered,
  hash-verified UK council election predictions committed to git with
  SHA-256 hashes before voting opened. 65,000-persona synthetic panel
  built on DYNAMICS-8; covers 136 councils. The repository preserves
  the predictions, hashes, scoring, and post-hoc honest reporting of
  KPM-1's headline result (28.5% per-council accuracy across n=130).
  KPM-1 is succeeded by KPM-2.2 v15.1 (council fragmentation, 59.2%)
  and KPM v17.10 (ward-level ensemble, 72.5%), both in the Kronaxis/kpm
  repository.
